DAY 1 – AWS (Scenario-Based Questions)

☁️ AWS – 15 Real-World Scenarios
	1.	Your EC2 cost suddenly doubled last month. How would you investigate and reduce it?
	2.	An application deployed on EC2 is unreachable, but the instance is running. How do you troubleshoot?
	3.	Your Auto Scaling Group is not scaling even though CPU is high. What could be wrong?
	4.	How would you design a highly available architecture for a web app in AWS?
	5.	S3 data was deleted accidentally. How would you recover it?
	6.	Your ALB is healthy, but traffic is not reaching the backend instances. What checks would you perform?
	7.	How do you manage multiple environments (dev, qa, prod) in AWS?
	8.	A Lambda function is timing out. How do you debug and fix it?
	9.	How would you secure secrets used by EC2, Lambda, and ECS?
	10.	You need zero-downtime deployment in AWS. Which services and strategy would you use?
	11.	How do you monitor application-level metrics beyond CPU & memory?
	12.	What happens if an AZ goes down? How do you design for it?
	13.	How would you restrict developers from deleting production resources?
	14.	You need to copy data across AWS accounts securely. How would you do it?
	15.	How do you troubleshoot slow performance in a VPC-based application?
